  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "62ccf0f8-60e5-4d53-97c6-2dc52bdfa070"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "grows paths that are shortest in every window of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ffab3c46-fde0-4c22-b6dd-2e4574ecb42c"],
 " edges. Unlike smooth geodesics, a germ has many continuations. We ask for \
the least ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2705052b-448b-4fb6-ab69-0d3292b318b4"],
 " at which the most visited paths become globally shortest: proposed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraGeodesicStraighteningScale", "[", "...", "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dfc9e1a5-2547-415a-b23f-dbe975f71cd9"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"1061e711-3800-4ce7-8e84-c58b334235c0"],

